%
O1001 (SQUARE)
(Using G0 which travels along dogleg path.)
(T10 D=0.375 CR=0.015 - ZMIN=-0.51 - bullnose end mill)
(T14 D=0.75 CR=0.015 - ZMIN=-0.01 - face mill)
N1 G90 G17(Tells Machine X,Y,Z Plane orientation)
N2 G20 (Imperial unit designation)
N3 M59 (Turn on Chip Conveyor)
(Face1)
N4 T14 M6 (Put Tool #14 in Spindle)
(2 FLUTE)
N5 T10 (Pre-Call tool 10 for quick change later)
N6 S2190 M3 (Turn Spindle on 2190 RPMs
N7 G54 (Work offset, where the part origin is positioned in the machine. Can have multiple offsets at once G54-G59 plus custom codes for more parts)
N8 M8 (Turn on Coolant)
N9 G0 X1.4769 Y-0.5888 (Rapid movement to a location just off of the stock material)
N10 G43 Z0.6 H14 (Height reference point for tool 14, Rapid .600 above Z origin point)
N11 Z0.2 (Rapid .200 above Z origin point)
N12 G1 Z-0.01 F51. (Feed .01 below origin point at 51 Inches/minute)
N13 G3 X1.4375 Y-0.6282 I0. J-0.0394 (Arc movement into part)
N14 G2 X1.0625 Y-1.0032 I-0.375 J0. (continue Arc movement into part)
N15 G1 X-1.0625 (Linear movement along X axis to end of stock)
N16 X-1.4375 (G1 remains modal, not needed for following block if a linear movement is used again. This movement moves the tool away from stock)
N17 G0 Z0.2 (Rapid above part)
N18 X1.4769 Y-0.159 (G0 remains modal, Move back to beginning X position offset on the Y axis to begin a new cut)
N19 G1 Z-0.01 F51. (Feed to .01 again)
N20 G3 X1.4375 Y-0.1984 I0. J-0.0394 (repeat arc movements going into G1 linear movement like before)
N21 G2 X1.0625 Y-0.5734 I-0.375 J0.
N22 G1 X-1.0625
